# Normalise text files to LF in the repository.
#
# Files are already stored with LF here, because this clone happens to have core.autocrlf=true.
# That is a per-developer setting, not a property of the repository: someone cloning with
# autocrlf=false on Windows would commit CRLF. This file makes the guarantee explicit.
#
# It matters most for shell scripts. The CI workflow runs `bash scripts/check-write-lock.sh` on
# Linux, and a script stored with CRLF fails there with `$'\r': command not found` — breaking the
# write-lock gate itself while looking like an unrelated CI glitch.

* text=auto

# Must be LF wherever they are checked out: these run under bash, including on Linux runners.
*.sh            text eol=lf
mvnw            text eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF.
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf

# Keep Java, config and docs LF everywhere so diffs stay clean across platforms.
*.java          text eol=lf
*.xml           text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.properties    text eol=lf

*.jar           binary
